  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of human rights and democratic reform in Aceh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lembaga Bantuan Hukum (LBH), the Legal Aid Foundation, provides free legal aid to people covering economic, social, civil and political rights. LBH also works to strengthen the capacity of communities which have become victims of human rights abuse, particularly in enabling people to stand up to any attempt to misuse the law to their disadvantage, and to promote an honest and fair judiciary system and judiciary process.  As a respected legal institution, LBH has played a key role in legal reform in Aceh, and has been supporting the local government in drawing up legislation. LBH has seven branch offices as well as its main office in Banda Aceh, and the CAFOD-supported project covers nine districts throughout Aceh.  As part of its overall strategy of helping the Acehnese people to restore the rule of law following a lengthy period of civil conflict (which only ended in 2005) LBH advocates for the setting up of a Truth and Reconciliation Commission after the model pioneered in South Africa in the 1990s.  This project is part of the Aceh Peace Programme.</narrative>
  </description>
